## The escrow state graph, and only the state graph -- money, the ledger,
## quote/timer orchestration, bank-webhook simulation, and the multi-step
## refund rollback all live in Elixir (see `lib/cure_exchange/`). See
## `README.md` for why the split is drawn exactly here.
##
##                       [ Created ]
##                            |
##                            | LockFunds(amount, quote_id)
##                            v
##                    [ FundsReserved ]
##                     /             \
##       QuoteExpired /               \ CounterpartyMatched(trade_id)
##                   v                 v
##              [ Cancelled ]      [ ExecutingSwap ]
##                                  /            \
##                 BankConfirmed   /              \ SettleTimeout / BankFailed
##                                v                v
##                          [ Completed ]     [ Refunding ]
##                                                 |
##                                                 | RefundCompleted
##                                                 v
##                                            [ Refunded ]
##
## Compiles (via `compile_cure`, a single-file `Cure.Compiler.compile_file`
## pass -- the same mechanism `examples/cure_turnstile` and
## `examples/cure_moneta` use) to `:"Cure.Main.EscrowFsm"`. Elixir drives it
## through that raw atom -- see `lib/cure_exchange/trade_worker.ex`.

use Std.Fsm

## The escrow's carried data: how much was reserved, which quote and
## counterparty trade it is bound to, and how many settlement attempts have
## been made (bumped by the Elixir side on each `SettleTimeout`; unused by
## the graph itself, but demonstrates that `data` can carry host-managed
## bookkeeping the FSM never inspects).
## `quote_id`/`trade_id` are `Atom` rather than `String`: they are opaque
## handles as far as this graph is concerned (never inspected, only stored
## and threaded through), and an `Atom` round-trips to/from Elixir as a bare
## atom with no wrapping -- unlike `String`, which is a nominal Cure type
## (`{String, code_points}`) that a plain Elixir binary or charlist does not
## satisfy.
rec EscrowData
  amount: Int
  quote_id: Atom
  trade_id: Atom
  attempts: Int

fsm EscrowFsm with EscrowData
  terminal Cancelled
  terminal Completed
  terminal Refunded

  Created --LockFunds(amount: Int, quote_id: Atom)--> FundsReserved
    when amount > 0
    update EscrowData{data | amount: amount, quote_id: quote_id}
  FundsReserved --QuoteExpired--> Cancelled
  FundsReserved --CounterpartyMatched(trade_id: Atom)--> ExecutingSwap
    update EscrowData{data | trade_id: trade_id}
  ExecutingSwap --BankConfirmed--> Completed
  ExecutingSwap --SettleTimeout--> Refunding
    update EscrowData{data | attempts: data.attempts + 1}
  ExecutingSwap --BankFailed--> Refunding
  Refunding --RefundCompleted--> Refunded
